{
  "chapter": "production/cost-engineering",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "The whole transcript is re-sent every turn, so the context at turn t is the prefix plus",
    "t-1 turns of history and total input tokens grow with the square of the turn count.",
    "Output grows linearly and gets the attention because the per-token price is bigger.",
    "Compaction caps what is re-sent, which is why it is a cost decision as much as a",
    "context one.",
    "The budget is enforced in the loop, not on a dashboard. Above the soft ratio the run",
    "degrades — cheaper rates, same work — and only stops when the next turn genuinely will",
    "not fit. A refused turn is not billed.",
    "Stopping is not an error. The run finishes with what it has."
  ],
  "prices": {
    "inputMicrosPerToken": 3,
    "outputMicrosPerToken": 15,
    "degradedInputMicrosPerToken": 1,
    "degradedOutputMicrosPerToken": 5
  },
